<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43615" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sēna</span></b> , ae, f.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A town on the coast of Umbria</i>, <i>where Hasdrubal was defeated by M. Livius Salinator</i> (547
			A.U.C.), now <i>Sinigaglia</i>, Liv 27, 46 sq.;
					<i><span class="en">Eutr. 3, 10</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sēnānus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of
			Sena</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aquae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
						Aur. Tard. 2, 1, 48</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sēnensis</span></b> ,
			e, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Sena</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">populus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					27, 38</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">proelium,</span>”
				<i>in which Hasdrubal was defeated</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Brut. 18, 73</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A river near the town of Sena</i>, now <i>Cesano</i>, <i><span class="en">Sil. 8,
			455</span></i>; <i><span class="en">15,
			555</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 2, 407</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
